.TH KEYAUTH-SECURE 1 "September 2025" "MyWallet Toolkit 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keyauth-secure \- production-hardened authentication for Bitcoin private keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keyauth-secure.sh
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR label ]
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR timeout ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.RI [ command
.RI [ args... ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B keyauth-secure.sh
provides production-hardened authentication for Bitcoin private keys, similar to how sudo works for system privileges. It implements comprehensive security controls including defense-in-depth protection, input validation, and secure session management.

The authentication system ensures private keys never appear in command line arguments, shell history, or process lists. Keys are stored securely in memory with automatic timeout and proper cleanup on exit.

.B PRODUCTION SECURITY FEATURES:
.IP \(bu 4
Defense in depth with multiple security layers
.IP \(bu 4
Comprehensive input validation and sanitization
.IP \(bu 4
Race condition prevention with atomic operations
.IP \(bu 4
Memory protection and secure cleanup
.IP \(bu 4
Path traversal and injection attack prevention
.IP \(bu 4
Privilege isolation and capability dropping
.IP \(bu 4
Resource limits to prevent DoS attacks
.IP \(bu 4
Environment variable security monitoring

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode. Suppress informational output.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose mode. Show detailed operations and security checks.
.TP
.B \-l \fIlabel\fR
Key label/identifier for keyring storage (default: "default", alphanumeric only, max 64 characters)
.TP
.B \-c
Check/validate authentication status only. Don't run command. Exit code 0 if authenticated, 1 if not.
.TP
.B \-t \fItimeout\fR
Timeout in seconds for key storage (1-300, default: 60)
.TP
.B \-h
Show help message and exit.

.SH USAGE PATTERNS
.SS Method 1: Authenticate and Execute (Recommended)
.B keyauth-secure.sh
.I command
.RI [ args... ]

This method authenticates the user and immediately executes the specified command with access to the cached private key. Most secure approach.

.SS Method 2: Separate Authentication
.nf
.B keyauth-secure.sh
.I # Authenticate (prompts for private key)
.B command
.RI [ args... ]
.I # Command runs with cached key access
.fi

This method allows multiple commands to use the same cached authentication within the timeout period.

.SH SECURITY WORKFLOW
.IP 1. 4
Check if private key is already cached and valid
.IP 2. 4
If not cached, prompt for private key using secure input (no echo)
.IP 3. 4
Validate private key format (64 hexadecimal characters)
.IP 4. 4
Store key in secure keyring with specified timeout
.IP 5. 4
Execute requested command with authenticated environment
.IP 6. 4
Key automatically expires after timeout period

.SH AUTHENTICATION ENVIRONMENT
When a command is executed with authentication, these environment variables are set:
.TP
.B BITCOIN_KEYRING_LABEL
The label used for key storage
.TP
.B BITCOIN_KEYRING_ACTIVE
Set to "1" to indicate authenticated context
.TP
.B BITCOIN_SESSION_ID
Unique session identifier

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Authenticate and send Bitcoin in one command:
.B keyauth-secure.sh send-secure.sh from_addr to_addr 50000
.TP
Check authentication status:
.B keyauth-secure.sh -c
.TP
Authenticate with custom label and timeout:
.B keyauth-secure.sh -l wallet1 -t 120
.TP
Verbose authentication check:
.B keyauth-secure.sh -v -c
.TP
Execute multiple commands with one authentication:
.nf
.B keyauth-secure.sh -t 300
.I # Authenticate once for 5 minutes
.B send-secure.sh from1 to1 10000
.B send-secure.sh from2 to2 20000
.fi

.SH INPUT VALIDATION
All inputs undergo comprehensive security validation:
.SS Label Validation
.IP \(bu 4
Maximum length: 64 characters
.IP \(bu 4
Allowed characters: alphanumeric, underscore, hyphen
.IP \(bu 4
No path traversal characters or special symbols

.SS Command Validation
.IP \(bu 4
Maximum command length: 1024 characters
.IP \(bu 4
Path validation for executable commands
.IP \(bu 4
Argument sanitization to prevent injection attacks
.IP \(bu 4
Executable permission verification

.SS Environment Security
.IP \(bu 4
Detection of suspicious environment variables (LD_PRELOAD, etc.)
.IP \(bu 4
Validation of PATH directories
.IP \(bu 4
Resource limit enforcement (ulimit)
.IP \(bu 4
Running as root prevention

